        "original_id": "4ecf020c-cb7d-5541-90f8-980af56f969b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Vanderbilt Yachts\n- Products: Holiday Mansion houseboats\n- Places: Chesapeake Bay, Florida coast, Maryland, Virginia, Atlantic Ocean, Delmarva Peninsula\n- Topics: boating popularity, estuaries\n\nFacts:\n- In their prime, Holiday Mansion houseboats were popular with lake boaters and coastal cruisers from the Chesapeake Bay to Florida’s coast.\n- In late 2004, Vanderbilt Yachts purchased the U.S. fiberglass houseboat brand Holiday Mansion.\n- The Chesapeake Bay is an estuary in the U.S. states of Maryland and Virginia.\n- The Chesapeake Bay lies inland from the Atlantic Ocean, with the North American mainland to its west and the Delmarva Peninsula to its east.",
